    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="1252" n="1094" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1094"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Thompson to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Yours 12th relative to American schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Hatteras</hi>,
                    second paragraph, article 5, of Mexican law, issued December 18, 1902, provides
                    a maritime belt of 20 kilometers in which vessels of all nationalities can be
                    inspected by Mexican men-of-war or coast patrol vessels. If the department
                    thinks this law should be questioned, will you kindly give further
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. E. Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
